ChatGPT said:

Yeah — this means the “unstuck” layer is not seeing the walls as blockers, or it’s too dumb at corners/doorways.

Two fixes that make this reliable without NavMesh:

Use your real cover mask from EnemySenses.cover_mask() at runtime (so even if your walls are actually on Layer 1, or your “cover” layers aren’t set perfectly, the AI uses what your project already considers cover).

When LOS is blocked, don’t only “wall-hug on hit” — also do a small directional probe (try a few rotated directions) and pick the best free direction. This is the classic “cheap pathing” that finds doors and corridors.

Below is a full enemy.gd replacement based on your current file (modules stay intact).

