Yep — what you’re seeing is exactly the classic limitation of the “simple tangent” wall-follow: it can “scrub” left/right forever on the first wall it hits, and never commits to going around corners / around the building.

So: EnemySenses is fine-ish, but your path brain needs to be upgraded from “tangent detour” to a real Bug / wall-follow:

When blocked, pick a side (left/right) and commit
Hug the wall using a probe that keeps a “hand” on the wall
Turn corners by updating the wall normal from probes
If it doesn’t make progress for a while, flip side
When it finds a doorway gap, step through it (this is the missing part in most naive implementations)

And yes: we should move this into a separate file so enemy.gd doesn’t become a goddamn novel.

