func point_blocked(p: Vector2) -> bool:
	return _senses.point_blocked(p)
Why this will now find exits “on the wrong side”

Because it’s no longer “tangent on first hit”.

It maintains:

a wall hand probe (keeps contact)
corner turning (forward probe updates normal)
gap detection (hand loses wall ⇒ step OUT through the gap)
progress flipping (if not getting closer for a while, flip direction)

That “gap detection” is the key for “door at bottom while player is top”.

One more thing you MUST ensure

Your cover objects (CoverFull/CoverWindow/CoverHalf) must be on the mask that the enemy uses:

Either set EnemySpec.tactical_cover_mask to include layers 9/10/11
Or rely on the fallback (the enemy.gd above does fallback)

So you’re safe either way.

